# InfraZero -- repository root
#
# Allowlist rather than blocklist: everything at the root is ignored, and the
# four source directories are then un-ignored explicitly. A blocklist quietly
# admits every new file dropped at the root; this admits nothing that was not
# named on purpose.
#
# Each of the four directories keeps its own .gitignore for what should not be
# committed from inside it (node_modules, .env, build output, datasets, model
# checkpoints). Those still apply -- this file only decides what is considered
# at all.

# 1. Ignore everything at the repository root.
/*

# 2. Re-admit this file, so the rule set is itself versioned.
!/.gitignore

# 3. Re-admit the four source directories.
!/backend/
!/frontend/
!/ml-pipeline/
!/simulation-engine/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the rule above deliberately excludes, and why
#
#   cluster-trace-microservices-v2021/    Alibaba's own fetch scripts. The
#   cluster-trace-microservices-v2022/    traces themselves are ~2TB and are
#                                         downloaded, never committed.
#   data/                                 Working data outside the pipeline.
#   output.txt                            Scratch output.
#   *.md at the root                      Project write-ups; the code
#                                         directories carry their own READMEs.
#   .sixth                                Editor/tool state.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Local environment and editor state, wherever they appear.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
